WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.467
Using REau day to day, with the bike and the dash

2
00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:10.133
1. Turn the bike on, open REau and tap Turn on. On Lite, turn the Android Auto server on first

3
00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:17.200
When Android Auto is active and the dash is ready, it is streaming. Put the phone away, with the screen off

4
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:23.867
2. With the bike stopped, set the destination in the Waze app, by voice or through the Android Auto screen

5
00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:30.733
3. On the Android Auto screen, tap and drag the picture to use Android Auto as in a car

6
00:00:30.733 --> 00:00:38.133
If Google Maps or the apps menu opens, choose Waze on this screen. After using it once, it tends to open directly

7
00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:47.400
4. On the joystick, in media control: left previous song, right next, up apps menu, down Gemini, center play or pause

8
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:55.267
In map mode, left and right move the focus and down confirms. Up is the dash's back and the center opens media control

9
00:00:55.267 --> 00:01:04.333
5. Calls: when ringing, left answers and right or center declines. During a call, center hangs up and up and down change the volume

10
00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:10.600
With the phone screen locked, the dash keeps going normally; only the preview inside the app stops

11
00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:17.467
6. If the dash's Wi-Fi drops, REau switches to Connecting and comes back by itself when the network reappears

12
00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:22.267
7. To finish, tap Turn off in the app or in the notification

13
00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:29.200
To go out again, tap Turn on. If Android Auto is still closing the session, wait up to a minute

14
00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.867
Have a good ride. On the road, eyes on the road

